        ("A direct comparison between two fundamentally dissimilar entities using the explicit comparison words 'like' or 'as' is a:", ["Simile", "Metaphor", "Personification", "Hyperbole"], 0, "A simile establishes an overt comparison using 'like' or 'as' (e.g. 'He was as brave as a lion').", "Figures of Speech"),
        ("An implied comparison that equates two unlike things directly without using 'like' or 'as' (e.g. 'The camel is the ship of the desert') is a:", ["Metaphor", "Simile", "Apostrophe", "Synecdoche"], 0, "A metaphor asserts an identity of attributes directly without comparative conjunctions.", "Literary Devices"),
