        ("A deliberate, extravagant exaggeration used for intense dramatic emphasis or comic effect is:", ["Hyperbole", "Litotes", "Euphemism", "Oxymoron"], 0, "Hyperbole magnifies reality far beyond literal truth (e.g. 'I've told you a million times').", "Literary Terms"),
        ("An intentional understatement formulated by denying the opposite (e.g. 'He is no fool' meaning he is very wise) is:", ["Litotes", "Hyperbole", "Paradox", "Euphemism"], 0, "Litotes emphasizes a positive attribute through ironical negative phrasing.", "Figures of Speech"),
