        ("A literary work in which characters, settings, and events operate as an extended metaphor symbolizing deeper moral, spiritual, or political truths is an:", ["Allegory", "Fable", "Parable", "Myth"], 0, "Allegories (e.g. George Orwell's 'Animal Farm', John Bunyan's 'The Pilgrim's Progress') convey sustained symbolic narratives.", "Literary Genres"),
