        ("A dignified, formal lyric poem written in an elevated, enthusiastic style to celebrate, praise, and honor a person, event, or object is an:", ["Ode", "Elegy", "Sonnet", "Satire"], 0, "Odes express intense emotional admiration (e.g. John Keats's 'Ode to a Nightingale').", "Lyric Poetry"),
        ("A narrative poem composed in short four-line stanzas (often with a refrain) originally designed to be sung, telling a tragic or heroic story, is a:", ["Ballad", "Epic", "Elegy", "Pastoral"], 0, "Folk and literary ballads tell rhythmic folklore tales of love, battle, betrayal, and the supernatural.", "Poetic Forms"),
