        ("The author's emotional attitude toward their subject matter, characters, or audience conveyed through word choice (diction) is the:", ["Tone (e.g. somber, sarcastic, celebratory, cynical)", "Mood", "Theme", "Setting"], 0, "Tone reflects the writer's voice and perspective, shaping reader interpretation.", "Literary Tone"),
        ("The prevailing emotional feeling, psychological ambiance, or sensory environment evoked in the reader by a literary work is the:", ["Mood (Atmosphere)", "Tone", "Diction", "Motif"], 0, "Mood describes the emotional atmosphere generated in the reader (e.g. eerie, joyful, melancholic).", "Atmosphere"),
        ("A literary technique that employs wit, irony, sarcasm, and ridicule to expose and criticize human folly, vice, and social corruption is:", ["Satire", "Eulogy", "Melodrama", "Farce"], 0, "Satire aims at moral reform by holding up societal hypocrisy, corruption, and absurdity to mockery.", "Satiric Literature"),
        ("A humorous or satirical literary imitation of the distinctive style, diction, and conventions of a serious author or genre is a:", ["Parody", "Allegory", "Pantomime", "Pastiche"], 0, "Parodies exaggerate stylistic mannerisms for comic critique or playful amusement.", "Literary Forms"),
        ("A novel constructed entirely in the form of letters, diary entries, or private correspondence exchanged between characters is an:", ["Epistolary Novel", "Picaresque novel", "Bildungsroman", "Gothic novel"], 0, "Epistolary fiction conveys raw personal immediacy through characters' direct epistolary voices.", "Prose Genres"),
        ("A coming-of-age novel that traces the psychological, moral, and emotional development of a young protagonist from youth to maturity is a:", ["Bildungsroman", "Novella", "Picaresque novel", "Gothic tale"], 0, "A Bildungsroman depicts self-discovery, identity struggles, and societal integration.", "Novel Forms"),
