        ("In Ama Ata Aidoo's play 'Anowa', the protagonist Anowa's tragic psychological decline stems from:", ["Her refusal to conform to patriarchal family expectations and her husband Kofi Ako's moral corruption through trading in enslaved people", "Her desire to become a politician", "Her lack of formal education", "Famine in the village"], 0, "Aidoo examines gender autonomy, historical complicity in slavery, and moral betrayal.", "African Drama"),
